#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every step is mechanical: the statements, their sections and the pages are all read off files, and the check either passes or names what is stale. Nothing here needs a judgement, so nothing leaves this lane."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For every statement extracted from the library entries the artifact draws on, read three things off files: the statement verbatim, the library entry it came from, and the section of that entry, as a library reference (layer, library id, section id). The section's label is read from the entry's structure: its title and its locator in the source's own unit (a slide, a page, a cell range, a line range). For example \"Catch up schedule, slide 7\". A statement whose section cannot be resolved is NOT published without a link: it is reported, because a statement nobody can trace is the failure this process exists to prevent."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Makes every statement extracted from a library source readable, with a link back to where it came from, in the folio's working artifact AND in the shared extraction viewer, and keeps the pages current. ONE SUB-PROCESS, CALLED FROM EVERY PROCESS THAT ADDS SOURCE DOCUMENTS TO A FOLIO'S WORKING ARTIFACT. Ingestion calls it when an entry is promoted; an authoring process calls it when it brings a further source into its artifact. Nothing here depends on the content type: a document, a paper, an implementation guide and a guideline all run the same four steps. What differs is how the artifact's pages look, and that is the content type's adapter's business, read off its content profile, never named here. WHAT A STATEMENT IS, for this process: a sentence or row captured verbatim from a library entry, whatever kind the extraction gave it (a recommendation, a requirement, a candidate still awaiting a person's ruling). It is published as captured, with its status; this process neither promotes nor edits it."
msgstr ""

