#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The generator's check mode regenerates in memory and fails on any difference from the committed pages, and on any source link that does not resolve. It runs in CI, so a change to an extraction or a library entry that was not republished fails the build rather than leaving a page that says something the extraction no longer does."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The same statements, with the same two links, are published in the shared extraction viewer, reachable from the site's sources menu. The viewer is the cross-artifact view: every source and every statement extracted from it, whichever artifact uses them. Both places read ONE collected list, so they cannot disagree about what was extracted or where it came from."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/publish-extracted-statements.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The statements are written into pages of the folio's working artifact, so a reader of the artifact finds them without leaving it. HOW the pages look is the content type's: its adapter renders them in its own format (pages of a document, a section of a paper, pages of an implementation guide), as its content profile declares. Each statement carries two links: to the library entry's page, and to the section, labelled as collected. The pages are GENERATED: a person edits the extraction or the source, never the page."
msgstr ""

